---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise"}
  description={"About RCE-JEPA. World Coding is the subject. JEPA, a Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture, is the premise: predict a compact summary of a program, not its surface text. The checker decides. Measured floors stay labeled. H15 is unfinished."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE-JEPA (RCE is the Reality Code Engine; JEPA is a Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) keeps its name. The subject is World Coding. JEPA is the premise: predict a compact summary of a program instead of the next word-piece of text. The proposer slot is any learned model over Forms. The checker decides. The Laws of Coding are the acceptance rule under test.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What it claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>It states a thesis, fifteen hypotheses (H1 to H15) and six falsifiers (RJ-F1 to RJ-F6). H15 compares proposer types on the ladder's residual of 40 tasks at equal energy. It is unfinished and has no measured result.</li>
        <li>Measured floors that need no learned proposer: median rho 9.34 over 185 hand-written programs (H1); 0 invariant violations in 1,275 fuzzed mutants (H7); 0 replay mismatches on 10,500 streams across six targets (H8); the plain arm of ladder run 3 closed 111 of 151 tasks (73.5%) with zero model calls and left 40, with 1 of 41 changes from real history (H14 supported by its registered rule).</li>
        <li>No learned proposer has been trained. The survey of other proposers is building-phase reading of published reports. The model only proposes and the checker decides.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><picture><source type="image/svg+xml" srcset="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.svg" /><img src="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.png" alt="The proposed RCE-JEPA pipeline: intent to a latent point, decoded to candidate Forms, each admitted by the checker or reported as requiring change." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The proposed pipeline. Any learned proposer may suggest a Form. JEPA, predicting in a latent space, is the instance drawn. The checker admits each candidate or reports that it requires change, naming the rule.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/rce-jepa/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/rce-jepa/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/rce-jepa.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/about/rce/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        Reality Code Engine →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
